      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Twitter/X</span><span class=\"chip company\">Instagram</span><span class=\"chip company\">Discord</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Distributed Unique ID Generator (Snowflake)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">How do thousands of servers hand out IDs that never collide, sort by time, and fit in 64 bits, without phoning each other for every ID? After this page you can design it, do the bit math on a whiteboard, and survive the \"what if the clock goes backwards?\" follow-up.</p>\n      "
